tp = nc['contributions']['tritium'] / nc['lcoe']
# § 3
body3 = f'''- **LCOE objective channel(s):** `{P}lifecycle_price__evaluate__lcoe` (the independent alternative, USD2004/MWh) with its eleven contribution channels `{P}lifecycle_accounts__evaluate__*_lcoe`; `{P}source_lifecycle_price__evaluate__lcoe` (the separately labelled source-conditioned diagnostic branch: supplied 1000 MW net unless the `source_net_power` axis sets our net, and the already-financed 5,055,773,960 USD2004 capital); `cost_ledger__evaluate__overnight`, `lifecycle_accounts__evaluate__financed_capital`, `cost_ledger__evaluate__annual_operating`, `lifecycle_accounts__evaluate__external_shortfall`, `plant_ledger__evaluate__net_electric`.
- **LCOE result:** the canonical 891 MW alternative gives **{f(nc['lcoe'], 3)} USD2004/MWh under `no-breeding-credit`** (tritium purchases {f(nc['contributions']['tritium'], 3)}, {tp:.1%} of the total; financed capital {f(nc['contributions']['capital'], 3)}; O&M {f(nc['contributions']['om'], 3)}; dated replacements {f(nc['contributions']['replacement'], 3)}; overhaul {f(nc['contributions']['other_overhaul'], 3)}; terminal {f(nc['contributions']['terminal'], 3)} less salvage {f(-nc['contributions']['salvage'], 3)}; consumables {f(nc['contributions']['consumables'], 3)}; deuterium {f(nc['contributions']['deuterium'], 3)}) and **{f(fd['lcoe'], 3)} under `assumed-new-tritium-feed-100`** (tritium {f(fd['contributions']['tritium'], 3)} for the residual {f(fd['external_kg'], 3)} kg/year purchase; supply service {f(fd['contributions']['supply'], 3)}; everything else unchanged). Both points satisfy every evaluated check. Overnight capital {f(nc['overnight'] / 1e6, 3)} MUSD2004 (direct {f(nc['direct'] / 1e6, 3)}), financed {f(nc['financed'] / 1e6, 3)} after one midpoint construction adjustment of {f(nc['idc'] / 1e6, 3)}; annual delivered electricity {f(nc['annual_mwh'], 0)} MWh at 0.85; annual operating cost {f(nc['annual_operating'] / 1e6, 1)} MUSD2004/year (no credit; O&M 70.0, external tritium {f(nc['tritium_cost'] / 1e6, 1)} for {f(nc['external_kg'], 3)} kg/year at 30 MUSD/kg, deuterium {f(nc['deuterium_cost'] / 1e6, 3)}, consumables 5.0) or {f(fd['annual_operating'] / 1e6, 1)} (feed100, plus the 30 MUSD/year service charge outside that channel); six dated blanket/divertor/LiPb events of {f(nc['event_cost'] / 1e6, 3)} MUSD2004 (PV {f(nc['pv_replacement'] / 1e6, 3)}); an other-equipment overhaul of {f(nc['overhaul'] / 1e6, 3)} at year 20; gross terminal {f(nc['gross_terminal'] / 1e6, 3)} less salvage {f(nc['salvage'] / 1e6, 3)} at year 40. The source-conditioned branch reads {f(nc['branch_lcoe'], 3)} (no credit) and {f(fd['branch_lcoe'], 3)} (feed100); it is a diagnostic, never the prediction.

**Over the studied space.** Against the 423 MW assumed baseline the alternative is cheaper per MWh without breeding credit ({f(bn['lcoe'], 3)} → {f(nc['lcoe'], 3)}, Δ {f(a_nc['delta'], 3)}: tritium {f(a_nc['by_contribution']['tritium'], 3)}, capital {f(a_nc['by_contribution']['capital'], 3)}, O&M {f(a_nc['by_contribution']['om'], 3)}, the other seven contributions {f(rest(a_nc), 3)} together) and **more expensive under the fixed 100 kg/year feed** ({f(bf['lcoe'], 3)} → {f(fd['lcoe'], 3)}, Δ {f(a_fd['delta'], 3)}: tritium {f(a_fd['by_contribution']['tritium'], 3)} because the fixed feed covers {f(fd['external_kg'] - bf['external_kg'], 3)} kg/year less of the larger makeup, supply {f(a_fd['by_contribution']['supply'], 3)}, capital {f(a_fd['by_contribution']['capital'], 3)}, O&M {f(a_fd['by_contribution']['om'], 3)}, the rest {f(rest(a_fd), 3)}); the ordering is set by the supply assumption, not by the plant. The unscaled-mapping control differs by {f(a_un['delta'], 3)} USD2004/MWh (capital {f(a_un['by_contribution']['capital'], 3)}: the two pump purchases). The changed equipment itself is worth little: the compressor rating moves the LCOE by 0.076 per 100 MW and its E4 price range by ±{f(abs(D['sens-compressor-price-1.5']['delta_lcoe']), 3)}. The aligned-convention ladder (§ 6, `results/attribution.md` § C) reduces the gap to the published 77.6 USD2004/MWh from {f(fd['gap_ours_vs_published'] if 'gap_ours_vs_published' in fd else fd['lcoe'] - 77.6, 3)} (feed100, our conventions) to a band that brackets it: with self-sufficient tritium, target-derived O&M, 47 calendar years and the source replacement cadence, our LCOE is {f(L7['lcoe_ours'], 3)} at 5 % real ({f(disc['0.00']['lcoe_ours'], 3)} / {f(disc['0.03']['lcoe_ours'], 3)} / {f(disc['0.08']['lcoe_ours'], 3)} / {f(disc['0.10']['lcoe_ours'], 3)} at 0 / 3 / 8 / 10 %) and the branch at 1000 MW gives {f(L7['lcoe_branch'], 3)} ({f(disc['0.00']['lcoe_branch'], 3)} / {f(disc['0.03']['lcoe_branch'], 3)} / {f(disc['0.08']['lcoe_branch'], 3)} / {f(disc['0.10']['lcoe_branch'], 3)}); the source's rate is not printed and no rate is designated as the match. Capital scope is a near-wash (the branch at our net differs from our own accounting by {f(br['diag-L1-source-capital-at-our-net-feed100']['capital_scope_effect'], 3)}: our direct × 1.49 × 1.1576 against the source's × 1.93); the denominator (1000 against 891.002 MW) is worth {f(br['diag-L1-source-capital-at-our-net-feed100']['denominator_effect_at_source_capital'], 3)} at feed100 and {f(br['diag-L7-aligned-combined-at-our-net']['denominator_effect_at_source_capital'], 3)} in the aligned case. The sensitivities (§ 6) show tritium price and feed moving the result by hundreds of USD2004/MWh, availability and the discount rate by tens, and the bounds on the unresolved recuperator, cycle-side and PbLi-pumping costs by {f(D['sens-conversion-services-6']['delta_lcoe'], 2)}, {f(D['sens-cycle-side-2.0']['delta_lcoe'], 2)} and {f(D['sens-pbli-pump-30MW-feed100']['delta_lcoe'], 2)} at their upper values.'''
replace(3, body3)
